{"title":"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also:\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also:</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is chosen randomly and uniformly from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed3fd299f7f005431bef3d44f28cf5f7494b169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-20, 18]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. The probability that the roots of the polynomial\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52637c1a16ba1c8d7606658b557d04191d8bcc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 + 2ax^3 + (2a - 2)x^2 + (-4a + 3)x - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"322\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>are all real can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524d9b869d9ee2d8b923afa9ce7c2c36bd9489e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The polynomial we are given is rather complicated, so let's use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_Root_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rational Root Theorem\">Rational Root Theorem</a> to see if the polynomail has any rational roots. By the Rational Root Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031656e5075aabc5b81126531273c38760866a51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1, -1, 2, -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" /> are all possible rational roots. Upon plugging these roots into the polynomial, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f361efa9ea92a34219e05e0825907161f273f17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -2$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> make the polynomial equal to 0 and thus are roots that can be factored out.\n</p><p>The polynomial becomes:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/2/9d25653483836820471a6a8561cacc9ef4cffbd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 1)(x + 2)(x^2 + (2a - 1)x + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"270\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Since we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> are real numbers, we only need to focus on the quadratic.\n</p><p>Set the discriminant of the quadratic greater than or equal to 0 to ensure the remaining roots are real.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/8/968d5a0a068dd820200478a2ad992bce4fb4b055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2a - 1)^2 - 4 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>This simplifies to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/8/058d194a0a1a498652aac06fe8658cdbf794920e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\geq \\dfrac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/b/c2b39d12e5518a75ed6756a91030b3a899a0cebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leq -\\dfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"59\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>This means that the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f0634e6e4d1c1a2144e333f98ddc60a904de91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(-\\dfrac{1}{2}, \\dfrac{3}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"71\" height=\"43\" /> is the \"bad\" interval. The length of the interval where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be chosen from is 38 units long, while the \"bad\" interval is 2 units long. Therefore, the \"good\" interval is 36 units long.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be97619dfd798600540322eca9ac7194806c6c4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{36}{38} = \\dfrac{18}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5a4831bb8e82f637bb1c3c9f950dffb87fbfe22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18 + 19 = \\boxed{037}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~First\n</p><p>~Somewhat minor edits by DaCow\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution is essentially the same as solution 1, but it offers a different approach to factoring the polynomial. \n</p><p>We want to isolate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so we rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52637c1a16ba1c8d7606658b557d04191d8bcc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 + 2ax^3 + (2a - 2)x^2 + (-4a + 3)x - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"322\" height=\"19\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf61b886dc5b9a3dc21f597f061bce4566857131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-2x^2+3x-2+2ax^3+2ax^2-4ax$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"311\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> are roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c593327913646c8e11d6d6f31f58a619321eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4-2x^2+3x-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />, so we can factor, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88f42a5178aa28a273190a87b72500bfcbc55e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)(x+2)(x^2-x+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We can factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/773fa1d7f171803e942eabdc00040b823fceac49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ax$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> from the other part of the polynomial, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/557742e9b32f42967855926c07ea0bc6d7f7d5f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ax(x^2+x-2)=2ax(x-1)(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"292\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, \n</p><p>\\begin{align}\nx^4 + 2ax^3 + (2a - 2)x^2 + (-4a + 3)x - 2 &amp;= x^4-2x^2+3x-2+2ax^3+2ax^2-4ax \\\\ \n&amp;= (x-1)(x+2)(x^2-x+1) + 2ax(x-1)(x+2)\\\\\n&amp;= (x-1)(x+2)(x^2+(2a-1)x+1). \\\\\n\\end{align}\n</p><p>The rest of the steps are the same as in Solution 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q2oc7n-n6aA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q2oc7n-n6aA</a>\n~Shreyas S\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also:\">See Also:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II\" title=\"2018 AIME II\">2018 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2018\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190113\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.101 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 227/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5341/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.065      1 -total\n 61.22%    8.611      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.16%    5.226      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16121:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190113 and revision id 292321. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}